WEBVTT

00:50.551 --> 00:51.385
Hey.

00:52.678 --> 00:54.930
You're not treating Eui-ju like that
on purpose, are you?

00:55.723 --> 00:56.599
Like what?

00:57.308 --> 01:00.478
She told me she thinks
the essay and demerits are unfair.

01:01.187 --> 01:03.355
You're not doing that
because of the filming, right?

01:04.190 --> 01:05.024
Me?

01:05.775 --> 01:06.859
You wouldn't, right?

01:07.693 --> 01:09.653
I'm pretty sure that was all
just a misunderstanding.

01:13.449 --> 01:14.700
I know she didn't film us.

01:18.704 --> 01:19.789
Then why are you doing it?

01:20.664 --> 01:23.042
Why are you being so strict with just her?

01:25.586 --> 01:27.004
I can't accept her…

01:28.714 --> 01:31.050
only getting four points in math.

01:37.223 --> 01:38.057
Have some breakfast.

01:39.225 --> 01:41.852
I hear after-school classes don't happen
unless five kids sign up.

01:41.936 --> 01:42.853
I only have four.

01:43.938 --> 01:45.731
I heard yesterday, Woo-su already has ten.

01:52.488 --> 01:54.281
Oh, you found your glasses.

01:54.365 --> 01:55.866
Took you long enough to notice.

01:55.950 --> 01:56.951
Dude!

01:57.034 --> 01:58.619
What's going on? You found them.

01:59.703 --> 02:02.081
-Where did you find them?
-Did someone see your flyer?

02:02.873 --> 02:03.958
How much did you give them?

02:04.959 --> 02:05.918
Why would I give any?

02:06.585 --> 02:07.545
Look at this punk.

02:07.628 --> 02:09.129
The person didn't want a reward.

02:09.213 --> 02:10.256
-What?
-Why not?

02:11.382 --> 02:12.216
Who knows?

02:14.343 --> 02:15.678
What a lifesaver.

02:16.303 --> 02:17.680
You should bow to them, dude.

02:18.430 --> 02:21.600
You should express your gratitude
to bring more blessings back to yourself.

02:21.684 --> 02:23.602
Yeah, dude, it's the least you can do.

02:23.686 --> 02:26.188
-Otherwise you'll get pooped on again.
-Yeah, dude.

02:27.398 --> 02:29.066
CHAPTER 15:
BLINK TWICE IF YOU'RE HERE UNDER DURESS

02:29.149 --> 02:32.111
Is it just me or does your heart burst
every time Yoon picks up his pen?

02:32.194 --> 02:34.280
Even Si-on's breathing gets me
right in the feels.

02:34.363 --> 02:36.490
I wish I could be tied up
with that leather watch on Yoon's wrist.

02:36.574 --> 02:39.118
The way that Tae-ha looks at Yoon.
Is he for real?

02:50.254 --> 02:51.255
Hi.

02:51.338 --> 02:52.923
What's so funny?

02:53.007 --> 02:55.217
What? Well…

02:55.301 --> 02:56.760
The new thing I uploaded

02:57.386 --> 02:58.679
is causing quite a stir.

02:58.762 --> 03:00.598
Really? Show me.

03:01.307 --> 03:02.766
I can't, it's embarrassing. Sorry.

03:04.351 --> 03:06.437
The way you're being
so secretive about it…

03:08.480 --> 03:09.607
Is it R-rated?

03:13.402 --> 03:15.279
No, don't be silly.

03:18.365 --> 03:21.493
It's not like BL, is it?

03:22.953 --> 03:24.204
BL?

03:24.288 --> 03:25.915
Yeah, you know,

03:25.998 --> 03:27.458
men liking other men.

03:29.668 --> 03:31.045
Oh, BL.

03:31.670 --> 03:33.297
I have heard of that.

03:35.507 --> 03:37.843
I don't get people
who like that kind of stuff.

03:40.387 --> 03:41.221
Of course.

03:42.264 --> 03:43.474
You're right.

03:44.099 --> 03:47.603
If it's a romance, why pair two guys
instead of a guy and a girl?

03:48.520 --> 03:49.855
What's so fun about that?

03:51.649 --> 03:52.816
Right.

03:54.735 --> 03:55.653
Right.

03:57.529 --> 03:59.073
The weather's great, isn't it?

03:59.698 --> 04:00.532
Yeah.

04:01.450 --> 04:03.035
What's our first period?

04:09.291 --> 04:10.709
My dad always said…

04:12.920 --> 04:15.005
When faced with a difficult choice…

04:17.591 --> 04:18.717
Is that your application form?

04:19.510 --> 04:21.136
Finally got my fifth person.

04:21.220 --> 04:22.763
This is going to be an elite team.

04:23.347 --> 04:25.307
Let's do this,
rising star of the athletic world!

04:27.518 --> 04:28.769
Sorry, Mr. Jung.

04:34.108 --> 04:36.110
Taking the more difficult path…

04:36.986 --> 04:38.946
is the way to salvation.

04:42.074 --> 04:45.577
Mr. Jung, I really wanted to do
after-school PE.

04:46.620 --> 04:48.122
But something came up.

04:48.205 --> 04:51.291
Blink twice if you're here under duress.

04:54.003 --> 04:55.462
She has a passion for math.

04:56.714 --> 04:59.049
She wants to get her score up
so I couldn't just say no.

05:00.634 --> 05:02.428
-Me?
-She should do what she's good at.

05:02.511 --> 05:04.596
Her long-distance running
is right up there.

05:05.097 --> 05:07.266
She obviously isn't an athletic type,
is she?

05:08.517 --> 05:10.227
Her face has got lazy written all over it.

05:11.061 --> 05:11.895
Me?

05:11.979 --> 05:12.855
No, it doesn't.

05:12.938 --> 05:14.356
I'm really hard-working.

05:14.440 --> 05:15.315
How much do you sleep?

05:17.901 --> 05:18.736
Ten hours.

05:21.196 --> 05:22.823
As long as you focus when you're awake.

05:23.741 --> 05:24.783
What rank are your grades?

05:27.870 --> 05:28.871
Ninth.

05:35.502 --> 05:37.087
Listen to your homeroom teacher.

05:39.590 --> 05:40.466
But, sir.

05:41.175 --> 05:43.510
They're not all nine.

05:56.315 --> 05:58.692
Today we're going to study the poem

05:58.776 --> 05:59.943
Invocation by Kim So-wol.

06:03.238 --> 06:05.783
INVOCATION

06:08.535 --> 06:10.621
KIM SO-WOL

06:14.708 --> 06:16.585
Let me read it aloud first.

06:17.252 --> 06:18.879
"A name which was shattered into pieces."

06:26.011 --> 06:28.180
Why doesn't Dong-ju
use the present I gave him?

06:30.390 --> 06:32.226
He probably doesn't want to burden you.

06:33.227 --> 06:36.355
If he uses it, you might feel obliged
to get him something else.

06:37.064 --> 06:37.940
Do you think?

06:41.443 --> 06:43.987
I'm going to tell him I like him
as soon as I turn 20.

06:45.823 --> 06:48.283
You really think
you'll still like him until then?

06:48.367 --> 06:50.828
You've never even lasted 200 days before.

06:50.911 --> 06:52.538
This time it's different.

06:54.623 --> 06:56.583
I'm really curious.

06:56.667 --> 06:58.836
Why do you like Mr. Yoon?

06:58.919 --> 07:00.087
Like what specifically?

07:00.170 --> 07:02.214
Not his looks.
There must be something special.

07:03.006 --> 07:04.675
Dong-ju

07:05.259 --> 07:06.093
is different.

07:08.095 --> 07:09.346
How is he different?

07:09.429 --> 07:11.515
Compared to all the other guys you dated.

07:20.149 --> 07:21.316
I feel sorry for him.

07:24.611 --> 07:25.445
What?

07:25.946 --> 07:27.197
I don't know.

07:27.281 --> 07:28.907
Just looking at his face

07:29.867 --> 07:30.742
makes me sad.

07:32.244 --> 07:33.871
It makes my heart ache.

07:39.376 --> 07:40.794
I guess.

07:40.878 --> 07:43.630
My mom said she married my dad
because she felt sorry for him.

07:43.714 --> 07:45.799
She also said never
to marry someone out of pity.

07:45.883 --> 07:48.218
That plenty of people
ruined their lives like that.

07:54.683 --> 07:56.852
But if you really like someone,

07:57.936 --> 07:59.605
I guess that's what it feels like.

08:00.189 --> 08:01.064
-Right?
-Yes.

08:04.193 --> 08:05.944
Feeling sorry for someone for no reason?

08:09.489 --> 08:11.617
I'm on cleaning duty again.

08:16.955 --> 08:18.916
-Good afternoon.
-Good afternoon.

08:20.584 --> 08:21.543
Great work today.

08:22.127 --> 08:24.379
Just look at that face.

08:24.463 --> 08:26.131
Who's ever going to feel sorry for him?

08:26.215 --> 08:28.258
Those on cleaning duty,
make sure you do it.

08:29.760 --> 08:32.304
No one, whatsoever.
For the rest of his life!

08:32.971 --> 08:33.847
Dismissed.

08:34.556 --> 08:36.642
-Thank you.
-Thank you.

08:39.394 --> 08:42.356
I can't say I'm surprised,
but he's a real freak.

08:42.439 --> 08:43.982
He hits you with demerits on a whim.

08:44.566 --> 08:45.859
And now after-school math too.

08:45.943 --> 08:47.527
He's the devil.

08:48.862 --> 08:50.864
Let's do it together.

08:52.699 --> 08:55.160
I'd follow you to hell.

08:56.495 --> 08:57.704
But after-school math? No.

08:58.664 --> 09:01.208
Punishing someone
with what they hate most.

09:01.291 --> 09:02.918
Honestly, it's genius. Right?

09:04.461 --> 09:05.504
Hey, girls.

09:05.587 --> 09:06.463
Do you have plans?

09:06.546 --> 09:08.215
-Not really.
-Nope.

09:08.298 --> 09:09.216
Why?

09:09.299 --> 09:12.219
I have detention cleaning
and then after-school class.

09:12.302 --> 09:13.303
Why do you ask?

09:15.180 --> 09:17.724
There's something I want to do
now that I'm in Korea.

09:17.808 --> 09:19.393
-What?
-What is it?

09:19.476 --> 09:20.852
What is it?

09:22.229 --> 09:24.523
CHAPTER 16:
MATH IS ABOUT PERSEVERANCE

09:39.246 --> 09:40.247
Mr. Jung.

09:40.789 --> 09:44.501
I guess all I can do
is gaze on you from afar.

09:46.169 --> 09:48.213
Is this unbearable pain in my heart

09:48.297 --> 09:49.965
because of a love that can never be?

09:50.882 --> 09:54.094
Why is fate so cruel to us?

09:54.803 --> 09:56.847
What are you doing here?
Do you have something to tell me?

09:58.557 --> 10:00.225
Mr. Ga forced you, right?

10:01.643 --> 10:03.103
Gosh.

10:03.186 --> 10:04.021
No.

10:05.063 --> 10:06.982
Let me help you.

10:07.065 --> 10:08.233
Don't worry about it.

10:09.318 --> 10:10.235
There's no need.

10:12.237 --> 10:13.238
Oh, come on.

10:13.905 --> 10:14.990
I said it's fine.

10:15.073 --> 10:16.074
Thanks.

10:20.037 --> 10:21.621
I'm not saying this for the sake of it.

10:21.705 --> 10:22.998
You're really talented.

10:25.417 --> 10:26.793
So feel free to ask me anything.

10:27.669 --> 10:29.338
If you need anything, just tell me.

10:30.380 --> 10:31.214
Okay.

10:35.969 --> 10:36.803
So…

10:37.763 --> 10:41.099
You competed in the singles luge

10:41.183 --> 10:45.312
until you were forced to retire
after fracturing your left shin.

10:46.980 --> 10:48.190
How did you know that?

10:49.066 --> 10:50.359
I read a news article about it.

10:51.818 --> 10:53.362
It doesn't affect my daily life.

10:53.445 --> 10:57.324
But you were forced to retire after
finishing fourth at the Winter Games.

10:57.407 --> 10:59.034
You must have a lot of regrets.

11:00.494 --> 11:01.370
Are you asking

11:02.329 --> 11:03.789
if I regret not having won a medal?

11:09.044 --> 11:11.129
There's something
more important than that.

11:12.089 --> 11:14.758
As I watched the medalists
from below the podium,

11:15.258 --> 11:16.426
I realized something.

11:17.844 --> 11:21.223
Despite all the sweat I shed to compete
in the Games, they must have shed more.

11:23.475 --> 11:24.851
I thought I was going to die.

11:26.728 --> 11:28.355
They must have felt the same, right?

11:36.196 --> 11:38.156
In that moment,
my placing no longer mattered.

11:40.242 --> 11:41.451
And above all,

11:45.831 --> 11:47.416
I'd kept my promise to myself.

11:50.585 --> 11:51.795
I never gave up.

11:52.921 --> 11:53.839
That's what counts.

11:57.801 --> 11:59.302
If I'd done after-school PE,

11:59.386 --> 12:02.264
we could have talked all the time
and gotten close.

12:03.723 --> 12:05.225
If it wasn't for Mr. Ga…

12:13.567 --> 12:14.985
-Hello?
-Where are you?

12:17.195 --> 12:19.448
Come to my office
and get the printouts for the class.

12:21.199 --> 12:22.617
Can't you get someone else to do it?

12:22.701 --> 12:23.869
I'm sure Ha-su would love to.

12:23.952 --> 12:25.662
But you're the TA
for this after-school class.

12:25.745 --> 12:26.621
Since when?

12:26.705 --> 12:27.706
You've got three minutes.

12:31.585 --> 12:33.420
Mr. Jung, I need to go.

12:33.503 --> 12:34.921
-You're leaving?
-Yes.

12:35.005 --> 12:36.173
Goodbye.

12:43.680 --> 12:45.557
She's top of class one.

12:46.349 --> 12:48.518
And she's top of class three.

12:49.186 --> 12:51.480
This class is the best of the best.

12:52.105 --> 12:53.732
I don't belong here at all.

13:06.786 --> 13:08.205
Are you here to bring us these?

13:12.042 --> 13:14.544
No, I'm taking this class too.

13:14.628 --> 13:16.463
You? Why?

13:18.715 --> 13:20.091
Mr. Ga told me I should.

13:21.218 --> 13:22.093
Mr. Ga?

13:22.886 --> 13:24.971
It's probably so we don't waste our time.

13:25.555 --> 13:26.932
It's better she does all that.

13:28.433 --> 13:29.809
Do you think?

13:29.893 --> 13:30.769
I guess.

13:31.811 --> 13:33.897
She got four points
in the September mock exam.

13:36.525 --> 13:37.692
Four points?

14:28.660 --> 14:29.494
Where are you going?

14:30.078 --> 14:30.912
Mr. Ga.

14:31.538 --> 14:33.540
Can't you just let me go?

14:33.623 --> 14:36.918
I'm too bad at math to be in this class.

14:37.002 --> 14:40.255
My old tutor and my cousin both told me

14:40.338 --> 14:42.632
I don't have a head for math.
I think they were right.

14:42.716 --> 14:46.678
I'm totally hopeless with numbers.

14:47.262 --> 14:48.680
Unlike subjects you can memorize,

14:48.763 --> 14:51.308
more effort doesn't always mean
better scores.

14:53.143 --> 14:54.394
Those four points.

14:54.477 --> 14:56.146
How did you get them? Did you just guess?

14:57.022 --> 14:58.356
No, I solved them.

15:18.627 --> 15:19.628
There you go!

15:19.711 --> 15:21.880
When Gauss estimated the number of primes,

15:21.963 --> 15:25.091
he spent years manually calculating
every single prime up to three million.

15:25.175 --> 15:27.177
Math is about perseverance,
and you have it in spades.

15:27.260 --> 15:29.429
So get back in there.

15:29.512 --> 15:30.555
But…

15:31.473 --> 15:33.558
Since angle CFA

15:34.142 --> 15:36.394
is equal to angle CAF,

15:37.312 --> 15:41.149
AC equals CF, which is 14.

15:42.525 --> 15:43.652
Now try and solve it.

15:59.834 --> 16:02.712
What the heck?
Why is she putting lip tint on?

16:03.296 --> 16:04.673
And during class at that.

16:05.507 --> 16:06.466
No way!

16:08.259 --> 16:09.260
Wow!

16:09.969 --> 16:11.680
I know they say
birds of a feather and all.

16:11.763 --> 16:14.683
Does she like Mr. Ga? Amazing!

16:23.692 --> 16:25.568
When am I going to write episode three?

16:37.622 --> 16:38.832
Yeo Eui-ju!

16:38.915 --> 16:39.749
Yes, sir!

16:40.542 --> 16:41.501
Yes.

16:42.085 --> 16:43.586
Aren't you going to write episode three?

16:45.088 --> 16:46.715
Episode three?

16:47.215 --> 16:48.049
Yes.

16:48.675 --> 16:49.759
Explain how it goes.

16:58.393 --> 17:01.062
Readers will probably expect

17:01.146 --> 17:05.817
Yoon to pay back the ten million won
in episode three,

17:07.444 --> 17:10.363
but the highlight of episode three
is the swoon-inducing scene

17:10.447 --> 17:12.157
between Si-on and Yoon.

17:12.240 --> 17:14.451
They're studying together
at Si-on's place,

17:15.034 --> 17:16.327
when Si-on says to Yoon,

17:17.454 --> 17:20.039
"You're really bad."

17:20.123 --> 17:22.459
"You keep making me think bad thoughts."

17:22.542 --> 17:23.543
Yoon replies,

17:24.127 --> 17:25.795
"Stop messing around."

17:25.879 --> 17:27.297
To which Si-on responds,

17:27.380 --> 17:29.716
"Do I look like I'm joking?"

17:29.799 --> 17:33.219
"I've never once joked with you!"

17:33.303 --> 17:35.263
…joked with you.

17:57.535 --> 18:00.580
Do the problems we covered in class today
and hand them in tomorrow.

18:01.414 --> 18:03.041
By tomorrow? How am I supposed…

18:07.504 --> 18:08.963
Damn it.

18:10.256 --> 18:14.719
CHAPTER 17:
JMT! (JUST A MARVELOUS TEACHER)

18:14.803 --> 18:17.055
There's something I want to do
now that I'm in Korea!

18:17.138 --> 18:19.265
GUESTHOUSE

18:19.349 --> 18:21.893
A pajama party!

18:28.650 --> 18:30.360
-Eui-ju!
-It's Eui-ju!

18:30.443 --> 18:31.569
Where have you been?

18:31.653 --> 18:33.238
Why are you so late?

18:33.321 --> 18:36.282
Is this the famous shaman's place?

18:36.366 --> 18:37.575
Be seated.

18:37.659 --> 18:39.244
How did you come to be here?

18:39.327 --> 18:41.204
-Is your name Yeo Eui-ju?
-Verily.

18:41.287 --> 18:42.288
Hello.

18:42.372 --> 18:43.832
-What took you so long?
-You're so late!

18:44.624 --> 18:46.626
Got you a present. Welcome!

18:46.709 --> 18:48.670
Oh, Eui-ju.

18:48.753 --> 18:49.754
So sweet!

18:49.838 --> 18:51.047
That's so cute!

18:51.130 --> 18:52.590
-Where's mine?
-It's really cute.

18:52.674 --> 18:54.592
-It's really cute.
-Thank you.

18:55.176 --> 18:56.553
Wow, you ate all this?

18:56.636 --> 18:57.929
-It's nothing.
-I'm bursting.

18:58.012 --> 18:59.722
Thus doth Kim Dan-ji proclaim.

18:59.806 --> 19:02.392
Eat like there's no tomorrow!

19:03.184 --> 19:04.269
I'm so full.

19:04.894 --> 19:06.104
What is that?

19:06.187 --> 19:07.689
Yeah! Now it's a party.

19:07.772 --> 19:08.982
-That's a must.
-Of course!

19:09.065 --> 19:11.317
Let me just make some space.

19:11.401 --> 19:13.528
-We always have a space for dessert!
-Rice cake sticks!

19:13.611 --> 19:14.529
Sweet potato.

19:14.612 --> 19:16.030
Let's go to the kitchen.

19:16.114 --> 19:16.990
Go to the kitchen!

19:17.073 --> 19:18.741
Let's go!

19:18.825 --> 19:20.827
Put this on before we go.

19:20.910 --> 19:21.744
This?

19:21.828 --> 19:24.414
Jenny, well done.

19:24.497 --> 19:26.457
Put them like this.

19:29.669 --> 19:30.879
And roast them.

19:32.338 --> 19:35.425
I'll show you the proper taste of Korea.

19:35.508 --> 19:37.510
I can't wait.

19:37.594 --> 19:39.679
Looks good, right?

19:39.762 --> 19:40.680
Yes.

19:41.848 --> 19:44.058
-It's really warm.
-It is, right?

19:46.769 --> 19:48.730
What? Do you need something?

19:49.856 --> 19:50.773
So…

19:53.109 --> 19:55.445
Hey, Jenny, by any chance,

19:57.155 --> 19:59.782
do you know A Night in Paris?

19:59.866 --> 20:01.117
A NIGHT IN PARIS

20:01.868 --> 20:03.995
You know that novel?

20:05.496 --> 20:08.207
Yeah, it used to be my favorite.

20:08.291 --> 20:13.171
The female protagonist, Isabelle,
meets her Brazilian boyfriend in Paris.

20:13.254 --> 20:14.964
At the Louvre.

20:15.048 --> 20:17.592
I did a double take
when I saw your messenger username.

20:17.675 --> 20:20.178
But what you told us about
how he asked you out was the same.

20:23.056 --> 20:25.475
So you knew all along.

20:25.558 --> 20:26.935
That I lied.

20:27.810 --> 20:29.479
Don't worry about it.

20:29.562 --> 20:31.731
Everyone wants to be the star
of their own novel.

20:31.814 --> 20:34.776
I just assumed you really like that novel.

20:36.110 --> 20:37.403
I don't really have a boyfriend.

20:37.987 --> 20:40.448
Everything I know about love
I learned from books.

20:42.158 --> 20:43.534
It's fine.

20:43.618 --> 20:44.994
It's no big deal.

20:45.578 --> 20:46.621
-Really?
-Yeah.

20:48.289 --> 20:50.166
I read it in translation first.

20:50.249 --> 20:52.794
And I really wanted to read the original.

20:52.877 --> 20:55.129
That's why I started learning Korean.

20:57.006 --> 21:00.468
You speak Korean this well
after learning from a novel?

21:01.678 --> 21:04.347
I read it so often
I practically memorized it.

21:07.016 --> 21:09.519
Do you like to read romance novels too?

21:09.602 --> 21:11.854
Well, you know.

21:12.480 --> 21:15.108
I started off by reading modern romances.

21:15.191 --> 21:18.820
Then I switched
to foreign romantic fantasy.

21:18.903 --> 21:20.196
And after that…

21:22.907 --> 21:23.992
And after that?

21:26.244 --> 21:27.787
Anyhow.

21:27.870 --> 21:30.707
Modern romance is the most mainstream.

21:32.750 --> 21:33.835
Right.

21:33.918 --> 21:37.630
I fell in love with Korea
after reading Korean romance web novels.

21:38.214 --> 21:40.299
Oh, I see.

21:41.175 --> 21:43.636
Which other novels did you enjoy?

21:45.847 --> 21:48.725
Fifty Shades of Mr. CEO.
Have you heard of it?

21:48.808 --> 21:50.643
-Of course! Have you read it?
-Yes!

21:51.310 --> 21:52.478
Did you read it too?

21:55.356 --> 21:56.232
-You did a great job.
-Looking good.

21:56.816 --> 21:58.943
-Hey, this rice cake is amazing.
-Stop it.

21:59.027 --> 22:00.278
You cooked these perfectly.

22:00.361 --> 22:02.155
Right? Have a bite.

22:02.780 --> 22:04.198
Oh, not yet.

22:04.282 --> 22:06.200
-Yeah, you need to add some kimchi.
-Sweet potatoes…

22:06.284 --> 22:08.619
-Kimchi?
-Yes, put it on top…

22:13.750 --> 22:15.126
How is it?

22:15.209 --> 22:16.794
-Wow!
-Isn't it great?

22:16.878 --> 22:17.962
Just marvelously tasty!

22:20.381 --> 22:21.966
You've got something on your face.

22:22.050 --> 22:24.177
-You've got something here as well.
-Come here.

22:24.260 --> 22:25.386
-Hey!
-No, I don't.

22:25.470 --> 22:27.055
Jenny, too.

22:27.138 --> 22:29.098
Hey!

22:30.266 --> 22:31.476
-With some grain syrup.
-Honey.

22:31.559 --> 22:33.102
-It's honey.
-Try it.

22:33.186 --> 22:34.103
It's good, right?

22:34.187 --> 22:35.480
-Do you like it?
-Isn't it great?

22:35.563 --> 22:37.565
This is just marvelously tasty too!

22:40.443 --> 22:41.903
This is nice.

22:41.986 --> 22:43.738
Man, I'm so full.

22:44.906 --> 22:46.699
Look at all those stars.

22:48.826 --> 22:51.579
There are so many of us, right?

22:52.955 --> 22:55.041
Like Mr. Ga said.

22:55.124 --> 22:57.168
We're all stars in the universe.

22:59.253 --> 23:02.799
When he says things like that,
doesn't he sound like the Little Prince?

23:03.508 --> 23:05.134
Know what I mean?

23:05.218 --> 23:08.221
Somewhere in the sky,
one of those shining stars belongs to me.

23:08.846 --> 23:10.890
And that star is speaking to me.

23:10.973 --> 23:12.225
Have you done your homework?

23:13.434 --> 23:15.394
-No!
-What is it?

23:18.147 --> 23:20.066
My math homework!

23:20.691 --> 23:22.652
No, my math homework.

23:22.735 --> 23:25.863
I couldn't even hang out properly
because of after-school math.

23:25.947 --> 23:27.406
When am I supposed to do my homework?

23:27.490 --> 23:29.075
I hate it.

23:29.158 --> 23:30.785
I hate it so much.

23:30.868 --> 23:33.121
Aren't you going to get more demerits
if you don't do it?

23:33.204 --> 23:35.540
-She's right.
-Whatever.

23:36.582 --> 23:37.750
What are you going to do?

23:37.834 --> 23:39.085
No idea.

23:39.168 --> 23:41.587
No idea, I don't care!

23:41.671 --> 23:44.841
Eui-ju, you've become gutsy.

23:44.924 --> 23:46.926
Did you see his face
when she faked being sick?

23:47.009 --> 23:48.553
-I remember.
-I know.

23:48.636 --> 23:50.304
He gave her a look of death.

23:50.763 --> 23:56.227
CHAPTER 18:
STRANGELY FAMILIAR, ALMOST MATHEMATICAL

24:05.027 --> 24:06.320
Mr. Ga.

24:07.947 --> 24:10.616
I couldn't do the homework.

24:11.159 --> 24:13.119
Can I just write out the solutions
ten times each?

24:13.202 --> 24:14.453
Did you even try?

24:17.540 --> 24:19.834
Keep trying until you can solve
at least one by yourself.

24:19.917 --> 24:21.586
Like you did on the mock exam.

24:22.712 --> 24:25.256
That only works sometimes.

24:25.339 --> 24:26.591
This isn't one of those times.

24:28.426 --> 24:29.260
Yeo Eui-ju.

24:30.720 --> 24:31.637
Yes, sir?

24:31.721 --> 24:33.514
What did I say math was on my first day?

24:40.188 --> 24:41.272
The universe.

24:44.358 --> 24:45.318
Euclid?

24:45.401 --> 24:46.819
In here, not during class.

24:56.370 --> 24:58.122
I said it's a subject
that requires thought.

25:00.124 --> 25:01.209
Yes, sir.

25:01.292 --> 25:03.794
You probably weren't paying attention.
Nor are you now.

25:08.049 --> 25:10.843
I thought solving one problem
would make you think.

25:12.887 --> 25:15.181
I didn't realize
you were such a lost cause.

25:18.476 --> 25:19.435
I'm very disappointed.

25:33.491 --> 25:34.784
I'm sorry.

25:48.130 --> 25:50.675
What on earth was he expecting of me
to be so disappointed?

25:52.677 --> 25:54.262
He even made me feel sorry for him.

25:58.641 --> 26:00.518
Still at least,
I got some dialogue out of it.

26:07.858 --> 26:10.361
So, how did he pay back the ten million?

26:10.444 --> 26:12.571
You keeping the rest
of this juicy story to yourself?

26:12.655 --> 26:13.823
Did she faint while writing?

26:13.906 --> 26:14.991
Give me my episode three!

26:15.074 --> 26:17.451
Episode three!

26:18.661 --> 26:20.705
The lines from Mr. Ga goes…

26:22.957 --> 26:24.667
I DIDN'T REALIZE YOU WERE SUCH…

26:26.294 --> 26:30.673
I'M VERY DISAPPOINTED, YOON

26:32.133 --> 26:34.385
I didn't realize
you were such a lost cause.

26:35.303 --> 26:37.096
I'm very disappointed, Yoon.

26:39.724 --> 26:40.725
Why?

26:45.438 --> 26:47.565
How can you read at a time like this?

26:51.068 --> 26:52.320
Stop messing around.

26:53.612 --> 26:55.740
Is Tae-ha gonna be waiting
outside your house again?

26:57.074 --> 26:58.159
YOON'S PAUSE INCENSES SI-ON

26:58.242 --> 26:59.201
I don't know.

27:00.202 --> 27:01.495
You're really bad.

27:04.665 --> 27:06.250
You keep making me think bad thoughts.

27:07.835 --> 27:10.546
I love it when you look at me, lying down.

27:10.629 --> 27:12.465
It makes me want to smush
my lips against yours.

27:12.548 --> 27:14.508
Until you can't breathe.

27:14.592 --> 27:16.510
SI-ON PRESSED AGAINST YOON,
HIS BREATHING RAGGED

27:29.190 --> 27:31.776
Now that's a proper cliffhanger.

27:31.859 --> 27:34.445
There's no way
you can skip the next episode.

27:49.126 --> 27:50.836
That smell

27:50.920 --> 27:53.798
isn't one I'm used to in the library.

27:56.133 --> 27:58.636
And yet, it's strangely familiar.
How should I put it…

27:58.719 --> 28:02.223
Like a skincare lotion
that a jerk would use.

28:03.057 --> 28:05.184
Almost…

28:06.435 --> 28:08.646
mathematical?

28:15.861 --> 28:17.530
I must be mistaken.

28:17.613 --> 28:19.824
Keep calm, Eui-ju.

28:21.409 --> 28:23.160
It's probably nothing.

28:24.286 --> 28:27.790
No, it's nothing.

28:47.143 --> 28:48.060
Move!

28:48.686 --> 28:49.895
Stay right there, Yeo Eui-ju!

28:51.564 --> 28:52.523
I mean,

28:55.025 --> 28:55.860
I.

28:57.236 --> 28:58.070
Muk.

30:15.814 --> 30:17.816
Subtitle: Paul Carver
